{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2097","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2097","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2097\",\"parent_revision\":\"788a2bf1665d5b2e5351ea48d60532c1750f9499d2d3649026420a21fe6f61d9\",\"root_revision\":\"788a2bf1665d5b2e5351ea48d60532c1750f9499d2d3649026420a21fe6f61d9\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: Add semantic (paraphrase) deduplication to research-curator entry creation\\nDate: 2026-05-03\\nGoal: Add an embedding-free cosine similarity helper (scripts/check_resource_duplicates.py) and update batch-mode.md to call it before spawning, so duplicate research entries caused by URL variants or paraphrased titles are caught at pre-spawn time.\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. Current dedup implementation is URL-string only (batch-mode.md line 67) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Fact-Check Claim 1 VERIFIED \u2014 file read confirmed \\\"Duplicate detection: Before spawning, check if ./research/ already contains an entry for the URL's resource.\\\"\\n2. Frontmatter field availability for similarity comparison | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: MISSING | Citation: Fact-Check Claim 4 REFUTED \u2014 414 total .md files; 37 have YAML `title:`, 11 have YAML `resource_url:`; ~280 non-insight entries use Markdown heading format (# Title, **Source URL**: <url>) not YAML frontmatter. The item's design targets `title:` and `resource_url:` frontmatter which covers only 11 entries.\\n3. Algorithm approach (token-overlap or character-trigram cosine similarity, Python stdlib only) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE\\n4. Similarity threshold (0.85 default, exposed as --threshold parameter) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE\\n5. CLI interface (--url, --against-vault, --threshold, JSON output format) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE\\n6. Target file location (.claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/check_resource_duplicates.py) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE\\n7. batch-mode.md Mermaid node to update (line 31: \\\"Parse deduplicated URLs from --batch\\\") | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE\\n8. SKILL.md integration scope | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Impact Radius confirmed SKILL.md Batch Mode Duplicate Detection subsection (lines 172-183) requires update; validate_research.py requires no change.\\n9. Existing test coverage for batch dedup step | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: filesystem check \u2014 scripts/ contains only backlink_lib.py and validate_research.py; zero test files.\\n10. (new) Fallback behavior when vault entries use Markdown heading format (not YAML frontmatter) | Status: MISSING | Missing: The item specifies frontmatter-based similarity but ~280 non-insight research entries use Markdown H1 headings and **Source URL**: body text instead of YAML title:/resource_url: fields. The implementation must define which entries to compare against and how to extract title+URL from Markdown-heading entries.\\n\\nChanges from snapshot:\\n- Condition 2: AVAILABLE \u2192 MISSING (Fact-Check Claim 4 REFUTED \u2014 vault entry format is not uniformly YAML frontmatter)\\n- Condition 8: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (Impact Radius confirmed SKILL.md scope)\\n- Condition 10: (new) MISSING \u2014 entry format heterogeneity not addressed in item spec\\n\\nAVAILABLE count: 7\\nDERIVABLE count: 0\\nMISSING count: 2 (conditions 2 and 10)\\nDecision: BLOCKED\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact Radius\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n### Code - Producers\\n\\n- `.claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/check_resource_duplicates.py` \u2014 new file; produces the embedding-free cosine similarity check. Does not exist yet. This script is the primary deliverable: implements URL canonicalization, token-overlap or character-trigram similarity, and JSON output. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Net-new surface with no prior coverage; algorithm correctness (threshold tuning, edge cases in URL canonicalization) has zero test coverage at creation time; any silent false-negative means duplicates still accumulate in the vault undetected.\\n\\n- `.claude/skills/research-curator/references/batch-mode.md` \u2014 owns the Mermaid wave-spawning diagram and the Error Handling prose section (line 67). Both the diagram node at line 31 (\\\"Parse deduplicated URLs from --batch\\\") and the Error Handling duplicate-detection block (line 67) describe current URL-only dedup behavior and must be updated to delegate to the new helper and document the `--threshold` parameter. | Risk: HIGH | Why: This is the authoritative procedure document; the orchestrator executes its Mermaid diagram as code. If the diagram is not updated before the helper exists, orchestrators continue using old URL-only dedup; if it is updated without the helper existing, orchestrators call a missing script \u2014 both produce wrong behavior.\\n\\n### Code - Consumers\\n\\n- `.claude/skills/research-curator/SKILL.md` \u2014 Batch Mode section (lines 159\u2013204) contains inline duplicate-detection prose that describes the current behavior: \\\"Before spawning, check if `./research/` already contains an entry for the URL's resource.\\\" This prose references the batch-mode.md reference document but also duplicates the dedup description in its own summary. If batch-mode.md is updated to call the helper but SKILL.md is not, the orchestrator reads contradictory guidance from two documents at once. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: SKILL.md loads before batch-mode.md in context; stale SKILL.md prose overrides or contradicts the updated batch-mode.md procedure for any agent that reads only SKILL.md; partial staleness causes inconsistent dedup behavior depending on which document the agent weighted more.\\n\\n- `.claude/agents/research-curator.md` \u2014 the agent file operates in a `--rerun` and `--fix` mode and does not contain batch logic, but it is spawned *by* the orchestrator after the dedup check passes. If the orchestrator changes the pre-spawn interface (e.g., passing a `--skip-duplicate` signal), this agent boundary definition must stay compatible. Also, its Boundaries section (line 515) states the agent must not coordinate batch operations \u2014 the new helper is an orchestrator-level concern, not an agent concern, and this boundary must not accidentally require the agent to call the helper. | Risk: LOW | Why: Agent does not implement dedup; boundary is clear; no interface change is required unless the orchestrator modifies what it passes into the agent prompt.\\n\\n### Code - Other References\\n\\n- `.claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/validate_research.py` \u2014 does not check for semantic duplicates (only structural validation of individual entries). It loads `backlink_lib.py` via `importlib.util` from the same sibling directory. `check_resource_duplicates.py` will be a PEP 723 sibling in the same `scripts/` directory; no import relationship exists, but the shebang/PEP 723 pattern must be consistent with the existing scripts. | Risk: LOW | Why: No code change required; the new script is an independent PEP 723 sibling; the only risk is convention drift if the new script deviates from the established pattern (shebang format, `typer` dependency, `ruamel.yaml` for any YAML parsing) observed in the two existing scripts.\\n\\n- `.claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/backlink_lib.py` \u2014 pure library, no dedup logic. No change required. Included because it establishes the code pattern (PEP 723 header, `marko` dependency, pure stdlib + single external dep) that `check_resource_duplicates.py` should follow for consistency. | Risk: LOW | Why: Not modified; serves only as a pattern reference.\\n\\n- `./research/` (vault directory, 37+ entries with `title:` and `resource_url:` frontmatter) \u2014 the vault is the data source the helper scans. The helper reads frontmatter fields. Any vault entries that are missing `title:` or have non-standard frontmatter will affect match quality. No vault entries need to be modified for the feature to ship, but vault schema consistency directly affects helper accuracy. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: If a substantial portion of entries lack `title:` or `subtitle:`, the token-overlap check degrades silently to near-zero similarity; duplicates continue to accumulate while the feature appears to work; the item description states \\\"37 entries have title:\\\" which means all current entries are covered, but future entries must continue populating this field.\\n\\n- `./research/README.md` \u2014 the README is updated by the orchestrator after every batch run (not by the new helper). No change required. Listed because it is the index consumed by `@research-cross-referencer` \u2014 if the new helper causes URLs to be skipped that would otherwise produce entries, README growth rate changes but no code change is needed. | Risk: LOW | Why: Informational only; no code path in README is affected.\\n\\n### Tests\\n\\n- No tests exist for any script in `.claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/` \u2014 confirmed by filesystem check. `validate_research.py` and `backlink_lib.py` have no corresponding test files in `tests/`. The new `check_resource_duplicates.py` will also ship without tests unless explicitly added. | Risk: HIGH | Why: The similarity algorithm (token-overlap or character-trigram cosine) has several correctness-critical edge cases \u2014 empty titles, very short titles (one-word overlap triggers false positive), Unicode normalization, URL canonicalization variants (http vs https, www vs apex, trailing slash, query strings). None of these will be caught by any automated gate without a test file. The item's own measurable signal (running the script against a known duplicate) is a manual verification step, not an automated regression guard.\\n\\n- `tests/test_validate_research.py` \u2014 does not exist. This pre-existing gap means there is no model for how to write tests for this script family. The new `check_resource_duplicates.py` test file will need to establish the pattern. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: Absence of existing test patterns increases the likelihood that tests are omitted or written incorrectly; the algorithm is deterministic and pure-Python, so unit tests are straightforward to write but require deliberate effort.\\n\\n### Documentation\\n\\n- `.claude/skills/research-curator/references/batch-mode.md` \u2014 the Error Handling section (line 67) states the current dedup behavior in prose. The Wave Spawning Mermaid node (line 31) names \\\"Parse deduplicated URLs from --batch\\\" as a pre-spawn step. Both must be updated: the Mermaid node needs a step that calls `check_resource_duplicates.py` (or delegates to it), and the Error Handling section must document the `--threshold` parameter, the JSON output format, and the skip message format. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Mermaid diagrams in this skill are declared as \\\"authoritative procedures\\\" and \\\"executed as code\\\" \u2014 stale diagram nodes directly cause orchestrators to execute wrong behavior.\\n\\n- `.claude/skills/research-curator/references/validation-rules.md` \u2014 documents what `validate_research.py` checks. The new helper is a pre-spawn check, not a validator, so this file does not need a new check definition. However, if the feature eventually includes a `--validate` mode integration (not in scope for this item), this file would need updating. Current scope: no change required. | Risk: LOW | Why: Out of scope unless validate mode is extended; no existing claim becomes stale.\\n\\n- `.claude/skills/research-curator/references/entry-template.md` \u2014 entry template describes the `title:` and `subtitle:` fields (used as similarity targets by the helper). No change required; the existing template already specifies these fields. | Risk: LOW | Why: Template fields are what the helper reads; no template content becomes stale.\\n\\n- `.claude/agents/research-insight-extractor.md` \u2014 system map table (line 60) maps \\\"Research workflows\\\" to `.claude/agents/research-curator.md` and `.claude/skills/research-curator/SKILL.md`. If the insight extractor is later run against a research entry describing the dedup helper itself, it will map correctly. No change required now. | Risk: LOW | Why: No current content becomes stale.\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n\\n- `.pre-commit-config.yaml` \u2014 the `ty` hook runs type checking on Python files (`types: [python]`). The new `check_resource_duplicates.py` is a PEP 723 script with a `#!/usr/bin/env -S uv run --quiet --script` shebang. Whether `ty` picks it up depends on whether it is detected as a Python file and whether its PEP 723 inline imports are resolvable in the ty environment. The existing scripts (`validate_research.py`, `backlink_lib.py`) are also PEP 723 files; if they are excluded from `ty` checking, the new file will also need to be excluded or have its deps resolvable. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: If `ty` type-checks the new script and cannot resolve PEP 723 inline deps, it will emit false import errors; if PEP 723 scripts are currently silently excluded, the new script will also be silently excluded and type safety will not be validated \u2014 both outcomes are invisible without deliberate verification.\\n\\n- `.pre-commit-config.yaml` \u2014 the `skilllint` hook validates `SKILL.md` and agent `.md` files. Adding a new script does not trigger skilllint. No change required to the hook. | Risk: LOW | Why: skilllint scope excludes scripts in `scripts/` directories.\\n\\n- `.pre-commit-config.yaml` \u2014 `check-executables-have-shebangs` and `check-shebang-scripts-are-executable` hooks will apply to `check_resource_duplicates.py`. The new script must have the correct PEP 723 shebang and be marked executable (`chmod +x`). Both existing scripts comply; the new one must as well. | Risk: LOW | Why: Pre-commit will reject the commit if the script lacks executable permission or a valid shebang \u2014 this is a shipping gate, not a silent failure.\\n\\n- No GitHub Actions CI workflow files exist (`.github/workflows/` is empty or absent). There is no CI pipeline that runs the scripts independently. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: No CI means no automated gate catches regressions in `validate_research.py`, `backlink_lib.py`, or the new `check_resource_duplicates.py` after merge; failures are only caught when a human or orchestrator runs the script manually.\\n\\n### Agent Instructions\\n\\n- `.claude/skills/research-curator/SKILL.md` \u2014 the \\\"Duplicate Detection\\\" subsection under Batch Mode (lines 172\u2013183) describes the current dedup behavior with specific prose about checking `./research/` for an existing entry. This is the primary agent-instruction surface for duplicate detection. When `check_resource_duplicates.py` ships, this section must instruct the orchestrator to call the helper script (with `--url`, `--against-vault`, `--threshold` arguments) and interpret its JSON output before deciding to skip or spawn. If the prose is not updated, the orchestrator will continue performing manual glob-based URL matching instead of using the helper. | Risk: HIGH | Why: Agent instructions are consumed at runtime; stale instructions cause the orchestrator to execute the old URL-only dedup path even after the new helper is available; the user gets no benefit from the new script.\\n\\n- `.claude/agents/research-curator.md` \u2014 no dedup logic in this agent; it operates post-spawn. No instruction update required for the agent itself. | Risk: LOW | Why: Agent boundary is clear; dedup is an orchestrator-level pre-spawn concern.\\n\\n- `.claude/agents/research-insight-extractor.md` \u2014 no reference to dedup behavior. No update required. | Risk: LOW | Why: Insight extractor reads completed entries; it is not in the pre-spawn path.\\n\\n- `.claude/agents/research-cross-referencer.md` \u2014 no reference to dedup behavior. No update required. | Risk: LOW | Why: Cross-referencer operates post-spawn; not in the dedup path.\\n\\n- `.claude/agents/research-utilization-assessor.md` \u2014 no reference to dedup behavior. No update required. | Risk: LOW | Why: Utilization assessor operates post-spawn; not in the dedup path.\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n- `.claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/check_resource_duplicates.py` | Role: producer | Connection: new script; primary deliverable of this item | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `.claude/skills/research-curator/references/batch-mode.md` | Role: agent-instruction | Connection: authoritative Mermaid procedure for wave spawning + Error Handling prose describing dedup; both require update | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `.claude/skills/research-curator/SKILL.md` | Role: agent-instruction | Connection: inline Duplicate Detection subsection describes current URL-only dedup; must be updated to reference helper invocation | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `./research/` (vault entries) | Role: other-reference | Connection: data source scanned by helper; `title:` and `subtitle:` frontmatter fields are the similarity targets | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `.pre-commit-config.yaml` (ty hook) | Role: ci | Connection: type checks Python scripts; new PEP 723 script must be compatible or explicitly excluded | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `.pre-commit-config.yaml` (check-executables + check-shebang hooks) | Role: ci | Connection: new script must have correct shebang and executable bit set | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n- `.claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/validate_research.py` | Role: other-reference | Connection: sibling PEP 723 script; establishes the pattern (shebang, deps, typer usage) the new script must follow | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n- `.claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/backlink_lib.py` | Role: other-reference | Connection: sibling PEP 723 library; establishes marko+stdlib pattern; no import relationship with new helper | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n- `.claude/skills/research-curator/references/validation-rules.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: documents validate_research.py checks; no new check added; no update required | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n- `.claude/skills/research-curator/references/entry-template.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: defines `title:` and `subtitle:` fields the helper reads; no change required | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n- `.claude/agents/research-curator.md` | Role: agent-instruction | Connection: spawned post-dedup-check; no dedup logic in this agent; boundary stays intact | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n- `.claude/agents/research-insight-extractor.md` | Role: agent-instruction | Connection: post-spawn; no dedup reference; no update required | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n- `.claude/agents/research-cross-referencer.md` | Role: agent-instruction | Connection: post-spawn; no dedup reference; no update required | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n- `.claude/agents/research-utilization-assessor.md` | Role: agent-instruction | Connection: post-spawn; no dedup reference; no update required | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n- `tests/` (no test files exist for any research-curator script) | Role: test | Connection: zero test coverage for the new algorithm and its edge cases; new tests required | Action: TEST_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH\\n\\n### Risk Summary\\n\\n- Overall system risk: HIGH\\n- Highest-risk systems:\\n  - `.claude/skills/research-curator/references/batch-mode.md` \u2014 authoritative Mermaid procedure treated as executable code; stale diagram causes orchestrators to execute wrong pre-spawn path regardless of what the helper does\\n  - `.claude/skills/research-curator/SKILL.md` \u2014 inline Duplicate Detection prose is the first agent-instruction context loaded; if not updated, it overrides the updated batch-mode.md procedure in any agent that weights SKILL.md higher\\n  - `check_resource_duplicates.py` (new) \u2014 algorithm correctness is untested; false negatives are silent (vault accumulates duplicates); false positives silently skip valid new entries\\n- Main risk themes:\\n  - documentation: two separate agent-instruction documents (SKILL.md + batch-mode.md) describe the dedup behavior; both must be updated atomically or partial staleness creates contradictory guidance\\n  - verification: zero test coverage for the similarity algorithm across any edge cases (empty title, single-word overlap, URL canonicalization variants, Unicode)\\n  - behavioral: the feature's correctness is entirely threshold-dependent; a 0.85 threshold is not empirically validated against the actual vault contents; false positive/negative rates are unknown until tested against real data\\n  - operational: no CI pipeline exists to catch regressions in any research-curator script after merge\\n- Scope expansion:\\n  - The item description focuses on batch-mode.md and the new script. The Impact Radius analysis found that SKILL.md contains a parallel duplicate-detection prose block that must also be updated \u2014 this was listed as DERIVABLE in the RT-ICA but is now confirmed as a required scope addition. The total documentation surface requiring update is two files (batch-mode.md + SKILL.md), not one.\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [ ] Every code producer updated or verified compatible \u2014 `check_resource_duplicates.py` written and follows PEP 723 pattern of siblings\\n- [ ] Every code consumer migrated or verified compatible \u2014 `SKILL.md` Duplicate Detection section updated to invoke helper; `batch-mode.md` Mermaid diagram and Error Handling prose updated\\n- [ ] Every affected test updated or new coverage added \u2014 new test file written covering URL canonicalization edge cases, similarity threshold boundary conditions, and JSON output format\\n- [ ] Every stale document updated \u2014 `batch-mode.md` Error Handling + Mermaid node updated; `SKILL.md` Duplicate Detection subsection updated\\n- [ ] Every affected config or CI path updated and validated \u2014 `ty` hook compatibility verified for new PEP 723 script; shebang + executable bit confirmed\\n- [ ] Every affected agent or skill instruction updated \u2014 `SKILL.md` Batch Mode Duplicate Detection subsection updated with helper invocation syntax\\n- [ ] Replacement or migration coverage gaps resolved \u2014 N/A (additive feature, not a replacement)\\n- [ ] Hidden transitive dependencies checked \u2014 vault frontmatter field consistency (`title:`) verified across all 37+ entries before relying on them as similarity targets\\n</div>\\n\\n## Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAlignment assessment: ALIGNED\\n\\n### Concerns\\n| Category | Proposed Change Excerpt | Mission Source Violated | Citation |\\n|----------|------------------------|-------------------------|----------|\\n| \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 |\\n\\n### Summary\\n0 concerns identified \u2014 proposed change is consistent with product mission and historical direction.\\n\\n### Rationale\\n\\n**Mission Alignment**: The research-curator skill's stated purpose (SKILL.md lines 1-4) is to \\\"Manage research entries in ./research/ \u2014 create, refresh, and validate.\\\" The proposed change directly strengthens the \\\"create\\\" phase by adding semantic (paraphrase) deduplication via `check_resource_duplicates.py`. This prevents the documented symptom: \\\"two batch invocations targeting the same underlying resource via different URLs (e.g., `https://github.com/espressif/esp-claw` and `https://esp-claw.com/`) will both pass the URL-equality check and produce two separate entries.\\\" Adding semantic similarity detection (token-overlap or character-trigram cosine similarity \u22650.85) aligns with the skill's vault-quality mission.\\n\\n**Design Principle Consistency**: The CLAUDE.md engineering stance states \\\"Every edit improves product design. Errors and linting issues are architectural signals \u2014 identify the systemic cause and log it.\\\" The proposed change identifies and fixes a systemic gap: batch-mode.md line 67 documents a duplicate-detection gate that exists in specification only, not implementation. The root-cause analysis (sections 10-11 of the backlog item) traces this to absent semantic analysis. Adding the helper script implements the documented gate rather than inventing new behavior.\\n\\n**Architectural Boundaries Preserved**: The proposed change respects the existing orchestrator/agent separation:\\n- Deduplication check runs at **orchestrator level** (pre-spawn, in batch-mode.md workflow)\\n- Research agents (`@research-curator`, `@research-insight-extractor`, etc.) remain **post-spawn consumers** with no dedup responsibilities\\n- This follows the established pattern in batch-mode.md where orchestrators handle coordination (wave spawning, progress reporting) and agents handle content work.\\n\\n**Historical Direction**: Merged PR #1964 (\\\"Implement automatic backlink detection for cross-references\\\", 2026-04-27) shows the skill actively expanding deduplication and relationship-detection capabilities. PR #435 (\\\"Enhance research-curator skill with detailed procedural diagrams\\\", 2026-03-05) established the pattern of updating batch-mode.md with Mermaid procedures. The proposed change follows this trajectory: strengthen entry-quality guarantees by detecting duplicates earlier (pre-spawn vs. post-validation).\\n\\n**Scope Consistency**: The proposed change is **additive** (adds a new helper script, updates orchestration prose) with no breaking changes to:\\n- Agent boundaries or interfaces\\n- Existing validation rules\\n- Entry template schema (continues to use `title:` and `subtitle:` frontmatter, already specified in entry-template.md)\\n- User-facing API (batch mode invocation syntax unchanged)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **add semantic (paraphrase) deduplication to research-curator entry creation** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/agent-frameworks/esp-claw.md \u2014 pattern: Semantic deduplication via embedding-free cosine similarity (Memory Optimization Techniques section)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-02\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n\\n<!-- artifact-gist:ce0dd8e3336741a4a78587b738f88734 -->\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-03)\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type**: defect\\n\\n**Rationale**: The item describes a traceable failure mechanism where duplicate research entries are created because the pre-spawn dedup check (batch-mode.md line 67) lacks semantic analysis. The cause chain is observable: URL-string comparison fails on mirrors and domain variants \u2192 both URLs spawn agents \u2192 duplicate entries accumulate in vault. This is not a recurring pattern (only one research-curator dedup item exists) and not missing-guardrail (the gate exists but is unimplemented, not entirely absent).\\n\\n**Analysis Method**: 5-whys root-cause analysis via /find-cause skill\\n\\n**Scenario Target**: Research batch invocation accepts mirror URLs (github.com and domain-specific) producing duplicate vault entries that fragment cross-references \u2192 Batch pre-spawn validates semantic equivalence (URL canonicalization + title cosine similarity \u22650.85) before spawning, so mirrors and variants are detected and skipped\\n\\n### Root-Cause Analysis\\n\\n**Method**: 5-whys via /find-cause skill\\n\\n**Evidence chain**:\\n\\n1. Observed failure: Two batch invocations with different URLs for the same resource both create separate research entries in ./research/ vault\\n\\n2. Why: The pre-spawn dedup check in batch-mode.md line 67 is documented but not implemented with semantic analysis\\n\\n3. Why: The dedup gate performs URL-string equality comparison only (batch-mode.md specifies \\\"check if ./research/ already contains an entry for the URL's resource\\\" without specifying HOW)\\n\\n4. Why: validate_research.py contains only structural validation (sections, headers, formatting); @research-curator agent workflow contains no entry-dedup step; zero code in research-curator/ implements semantic similarity checking\\n\\n5. Why: URL-string equality fails to catch semantically equivalent resources: \\\"https://github.com/espressif/esp-claw\\\" != \\\"https://esp-claw.com/\\\", \\\"http://example.com\\\" != \\\"https://example.com/\\\", etc.\\n\\n**Root cause**: The dedup validation gate specified in batch-mode.md is absent. No URL canonicalization, title matching, or semantic similarity check exists before spawning research agents. String equality comparison alone allows mirrors and domain variants to bypass dedup and create duplicate entries.\\n\\n**Fix locus**: batch-mode.md line 67 (the dedup check) + new file scripts/check_resource_duplicates.py (semantic analysis helper)\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`./.claude/skills/research-curator/references/batch-mode.md` line 67 specifies: \\\"Before spawning, check if `./research/` already contains an entry for the URL's resource. If found, skip with info message suggesting `--rerun` instead.\\\" Verified by Grep: only `batch-mode.md` line 31 mentions \\\"deduplicated URLs\\\" \u2014 deduplication is purely URL-string-based. Grep of `.claude/skills/research-curator/` for `cosine`, `similarity`, `semantic`, or `paraphrase` returns zero matches. The validate_research.py script and `@research-curator` agent perform no title/topic similarity check.\\n\\nSymptom: two batch invocations targeting the same underlying resource via different URLs (e.g., `https://github.com/espressif/esp-claw` and `https://esp-claw.com/`, or a mirror site and the canonical site) will both pass the URL-equality check and produce two separate entries describing the same project. The same applies to URL canonicalization variants (trailing slash, http vs https, www vs apex). The vault accumulates near-duplicate entries that fragment cross-references and waste reader time.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`./.claude/skills/research-curator/references/batch-mode.md` Wave Spawning step (the URL deduplication node) and the corresponding pre-spawn check delegate to a new helper `scripts/check_resource_duplicates.py` that performs:\\n\\n1. URL canonicalization (lowercase host, strip trailing slash, normalize www/non-www, strip query strings irrelevant to identity)\\n2. Title/topic similarity check against existing entries' frontmatter `title:` and `subtitle:` using a token-overlap or character-trigram cosine similarity (no embedding model required \u2014 same approach ESP-CLAW uses on its 400KB SRAM device)\\n3. If similarity >= 0.85, skip with info message \\\"Resource appears to match existing entry: {path}. Use `--rerun {category}/{name}` to refresh.\\\"\\n\\nField `similarity_threshold` exposed as a parameter (default 0.85) in the helper script and documented in `batch-mode.md`.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRun: `uv run .claude/skills/research-curator/scripts/check_resource_duplicates.py --url https://esp-claw.com/ --against-vault ./research/`. Output JSON includes `matches: [{path: \\\"agent-frameworks/esp-claw.md\\\", similarity: 0.92, reason: \\\"title token overlap\\\"}]` because `agent-fr